.TH CARBON\-BADGE 1 "2026-09" "carbon-badge" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
carbon-badge \- carbon cost of a repository's CI, as a badge
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B carbon-badge
.I REPO
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Prices a repository's CI minutes as grams of CO2e and emits a badge
endpoint for it. REPO is
.I owner/repo
on GitHub or
.I group/project
on GitLab.
.PP
Energy is estimated, not measured: neither API exposes runner utilisation or
size, so the runner's power draw is declared rather than detected. The
assumptions, and what they cost in accuracy, are documented in the project's
docs/assumptions.md.
.SH OPTIONS
.SS Source
.TP
.BI \-\-provider " NAME"
.B github
(default) or
.BR gitlab .
.TP
.BI \-\-api " URL"
Override the API base URL, for GitHub Enterprise or self-hosted GitLab.
.TP
.BI \-\-token " TOKEN"
API token. Prefer
.I GITHUB_TOKEN
or
.I GITLAB_TOKEN
in the environment, matching
.BR \-\-provider .
.TP
.BI \-\-minutes " N"
Skip the API and use this many CI minutes. For testing and offline use.
.SS Grid intensity
.TP
.BI \-\-grid\-intensity " G"
gCO2e per kWh applied to every job. Unset, each job that reported its
region is priced on that region's grid and the rest fall back to the world
average. Ignored when
.B \-\-grid\-region
is set.
.TP
.BI \-\-grid\-region " ZONE"
Electricity Maps zone, e.g.
.BR SE ,
.BR US-CAL-CISO ,
for live grid intensity.
.TP
.BI \-\-electricitymaps\-token " TOKEN"
Electricity Maps API token, or
.I ELECTRICITYMAPS_TOKEN
in the environment.
.TP
.BI \-\-eia\-key " KEY"
EIA API key, or
.I EIA_API_KEY
in the environment, to price US regions from their balancing authority's
live fuel mix. European and UK regions need no key.
.SS Power model
.TP
.BI \-\-runner\-watts " WATTS|LABEL=WATTS"
Average power draw of the runners. A bare number applies to every job;
.I LABEL=WATTS
is repeatable and only needed when runner types are mixed.
.TP
.BI \-\-load\-factor " F"
Average CPU utilisation of these jobs, 0\-1. The default of 1.0 prices
every job at full load, which overstates an I/O-bound job by up to about
three times. Only the variable part of the draw scales: at 0 a machine
still draws its idle power.
.SS Diagnostics and serving
.TP
.B \-\-ignore\-self\-reported
Query the API for every run, ignoring what jobs recorded about themselves.
Slower and no more accurate.
.TP
.B \-\-reconcile
Run both paths over the same runs and report where they disagree, split
into setup time, the watts model and the grid factor. A diagnostic, not a
badge.
.TP
.BI \-\-serve " PORT"
Serve
.I /badge.json
on this port instead of printing once and exiting.
.TP
.BI \-\-bind " ADDR"
Interface for
.BR \-\-serve .
The default is what a container needs; use 127.0.0.1 on a shared host.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
A badge was produced.
.TP
.B non-zero
The API could not be reached, or the arguments were rejected.
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
Price a repository's CI on the local grid:
.PP
.RS
.B carbon-badge fabiocicerchia/greenlint \-\-grid\-region SE
.RE
.PP
Serve the badge endpoint:
.PP
.RS
.B carbon-badge acme/api \-\-serve 8080
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR greenlint (1).
Project documentation:
.UR https://github.com/fabiocicerchia/carbon-badge
.UE
